#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""feb: your box (a persistent ROS 2 container), the simulator app and Foxglove, from one command.

    ./feb setup --name "Your Name"     once: Docker check, image, simulator app, the box
    ./feb up                           house nodes in the box + simulator + Foxglove, drive by hand
    ./feb up --track loop --stack "ros2 launch feb_driver drive.launch.py"
    ./feb up --stack "..." --opponent normal     race the house racer (slow | normal | fast | map)
    ./feb shell                        a terminal in the box (ROS sourced; open as many as you like)
    ./feb shell --gui                  ...and the box's desktop in your browser (rviz2, rqt, turtlesim)
    ./feb code                         VS Code attached to the box
    ./feb stop                         end `feb up` (the box stays)
    ./feb reset                        wipe the box; the next command makes a fresh one
    ./feb update                       git pull, newer image, newer simulator app
    ./feb practice --driver NAME       scored runs on the driver's practice set (its kind's tracks)
    ./feb submit                       post the clean runs to the scoreboard and the driver's code to feb-stack

The box mounts the folder that holds this clone (your FEB folder) at /home/feb/FEB and keeps
everything you install until `feb reset`. The simulator is a native app for your OS; it connects
to the box on port 4567. `run` is an alias of `up`.

Environment overrides: FEB_SIM_APP, FEB_DEVKIT_IMAGE, FEB_DEVKIT_GUI_IMAGE, FEB_BOX_NAME,
FEB_DEVKIT_PORT, FEB_FOXGLOVE_PORT, FEB_VNC_PORT.
"""
